Expected elements: MISSING — replay telemetry in the transaction pane

A presence failure, so it is finding #1 and my rating is capped at 4. Nowhere in this image do instructions-executed, effects-matched or `effectsMismatched: 0` appear. The pane runs Data → Block → Type → Age → Canonical → Finality → Cost → Executions → Decoded Input → Raw, then clips mid-`RAW (CHAIN-NATIVE)` at y1075. That telemetry is the page's only evidence the replay reproduced the chain's effects — off-screen on the view whose argument is that this data was not manufactured.

Otherwise the register holds and the source-less explanation is well written. Code (y129–194), Call Trace (y122) and Values (y723) each state the limit as a fact about Aztec contract classes, blame no recorder and apologise nowhere; `Supply sources` (66,298) makes it a route, not a wall. No gutter glyphs render at all — correct here.

But the copy defects earlier rounds found elsewhere are on this page. The provenance paragraph shouts `THIS CHAIN IS PUBLISHED AS A CURATED WINDOW.` (y283) inside sentence-case prose, carries the placeholder `32 transaction(s)` (y414), and prints the raw enum `(not-attempted)` (y501). The cost unit reads `mana (FeeJuice)` (y771): a gas unit and an asset in one string, camel-cased where the chain writes "Fee Juice".

Withdrawn on measurement: the fee no longer wraps as raw hex. It is one right-aligned decimal and the grid holds; 19 ungrouped digits remain unsizeable.

Fixes: telemetry above the fold; de-shout and de-placeholder the provenance paragraph.

Rating: 4/10

